Q: When i use Assert.assertFalse(), to check the absence of an element, my scripts are getting failed A: <p>I know this question is old but it's shown back up on the front page and doesn't have an accepted answer...</p>
<p>The problem with your assert is that if the element doesn't exist, Selenium throws the <code>NoSuchElementException</code>. To avoid this, use <code>.findElements()</code> (plural) and then check the size of the returned list. If the list contains an element, then check for visible. The code looks like the below.</p>
<pre><code>List&lt;WebElement&gt; e = driver.findElements(By.xpath(&quot;element's xpath&quot;));
if (!e.isEmpty()) {
    Assert.assertFalse(e.get(0).isDisplayed(), &quot;Bug!! The element is visible.&quot;);
}
</code></pre>

Q: how to show data from database to JTable of Java Swing Controls A: <p><strong>Use this code :</strong></p>

<pre><code>import java.awt.*;
import java.awt.event.*;
import java.sql.*;
import java.util.Vector;
import javax.swing.*;
import javax.swing.table.DefaultTableModel;

public class DisplayEmpData extends JFrame implements ActionListener {

